# Uint8Array.from.$call(Bun.serve, <a list>), as only the text of the library can write it
# Bun.serve may be handed an option that runs code which nobody has seen, and whether it is, is asked where it is called in sight or let go. It does not inherit %TypedArray%.from, so the rule on a
# receiver that is only constructed does not hold for it: it is let go, and code that nobody has seen can run.
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: causes
# CHECK: unseen-code can-run

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = NewArray contents=anything
    v1 = Builtin builtin=Uint8Array
    v2 = PropGet v1 key="from"
    v3 = Convert v2 declared={type=builtin(TypedArrayFrom) flags=[IsExpected]}
    v4 = Builtin builtin=BunServe
    v5 = Call v3, v4, v0
    Return v5
}
